<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>





<handout>
    <title>Learning Target 16 Practice</title>

    <p >
        <em>Given a statement to be proven using a proof by contradiction, identify the assumptions to be made and the statements to be proven.

        </em>
    </p>

   <paragraphs>
           <title>Need to know</title>
   
           <p>
               <ul>
                   <li>
                       <p>
                           How to negate conditional statements (e.g.
                           <q>if...then...</q> statements).
                       </p>
                   </li>
   
                   <li>
                       <p>
                           What to assume at the start of a proof by contradiction.
                       </p>
                   </li>
   
                   <li>
                       <p>
                           What a contradiction is at the end of a proof by contradiction, and examples of some common contradictions.
                       </p>
                   </li>
               </ul>
           </p>
        </paragraphs>
   
       <paragraphs>
           <title>Practice Questions</title>
   
          <exercise>
            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        Weekly Practice 11 (just what you assume and make note of the contradictions you arrive at)
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>
